data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":4252,"output_index":4,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_08c92b3bd58b185d016adf6fafe0948191a458b61b2d2fb0e8","call_id":"call_b3578d82240f43c0b3df131edf461e1e","name":"save_interface_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped ENNReal NNReal\\nabbrev V (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)\\nabbrev W (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n ⊕ Unit)\\nnoncomputable def pack (n : ℕ) (x : V n) (t : ℝ) : W n := WithLp.toLp 2 (Sum.elim (fun i => x i) (fun _ => t))\\nnoncomputable def projX (n : ℕ) (z : W n) : V n := WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i => z (Sum.inl i))\\nnoncomputable def projT (n : ℕ) (z : W n) : ℝ := z (Sum.inr ())\\ndef unitI : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 1\\ndef cyl (n : ℕ) (E : Set (V n)) : Set (W n) := {z | projX n z ∈ E ∧ projT n z ∈ unitI}\\nnoncomputable def coverCost {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (s : ℝ) (U : ℕ → Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ∑' i, ⨆ (_ : (U i).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s\\ndef IsCover {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) (U : ℕ → Set X) : Prop := A ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ ∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ\\nnoncomputable def Hscale {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (s δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ⨅ (U : ℕ → Set X) (_ : IsCover δ A U), coverCost s U\\nnoncomputable def Hmeasure {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := ⨆ (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ), Hscale s δ A\\nnoncomputable def Hnative {X : Type*} [MetricSpace X] (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ := letI : MeasurableSpace X := borel X; letI : BorelSpace X := ⟨rfl⟩; MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure s A\\n\",\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"n\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"E\",\"type\":\"Set (V n)\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"E.Nonempty\",\"H002\":\"IsCompact E\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"dimH (cyl n E) = dimH E + 1\",\"representation\":\"V n is Euclidean ℝ^n. W n is the Euclidean space with n coordinate indices and one final index, not the default max-metric product. pack and the two coordinate projections realize the product identification; cyl is exactly E×[0,1] in these coordinates, also at n=0. All dimensions use native dimH in ℝ≥0∞. Real exponents and scales remain real and positive in every obligation; ENNReal.ofReal embeds them. No real representative of dimH E is used before finiteness. Extended diameter is the extended supremum of distances, so finite scale rules out unbounded covering members. coverCost explicitly makes empty members zero. Hscale is the countable-cover infimum and Hmeasure the supremum over positive finite real scales. Hnative fixes the Borel measurable structure by a definitional local instance, with no additional hypothesis. Library Hausdorff and integration facts are used directly, not as premise ports. Semantic correspondence remains PENDING_AUDIT_B.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"∀ (X : Type*) [MetricSpace X] (A : Set X) (s : ℝ), 0 < s → Hmeasure s A = Hnative s A\",\"inputs\":[],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\"],\"explanation\":\"Apply hausdorffMeasure_apply with the Borel structure. Identify the finite real scales with positive finite ENNReal scales; the infinite scale contributes no larger infimum. On finite-scale covers ediam is the required ordinary diameter. Empty-member weights agree by definition.\"},{\"id\":\"T002\",\"statement\":\"∀ (X : Type*) [MetricSpace X] (A : Set X) (s : ℝ), 0 < s → Hmeasure s A = Hnative s A ∧ (dimH A < ENNReal.ofReal s → Hmeasure s A = 0) ∧ (ENNReal.ofReal s < dimH A → Hmeasure s A = ⊤) ∧ (Hmeasure s A = 0 → dimH A ≤ ENNReal.ofReal s) ∧ (Hmeasure s A = ⊤ → ENNReal.ofReal s ≤ dimH A)\",\"inputs\":[\"T001\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S002\"],\"explanation\":\"N001. Transfer the native critical-exponent lemmas through T001. Represent a positive real exponent as a nonnegative real for the library lemmas. The infinite-measure converse follows from the defining supremum of dimH.\"},{\"id\":\"T003\",\"statement\":\"Bornology.IsBounded E ∧ (∃ B : ℝ, 1 ≤ B ∧ ∀ x ∈ E, ‖x‖ ≤ B) ∧ (∀ (s δ : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → ∃ (k : ℕ) (U : Fin k → Set (V n)), E ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ (∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ) ∧ (∑ i, (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s) < ⊤) ∧ (∀ (s δ : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → Hscale s δ E < ⊤)\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S003\"],\"explanation\":\"Compactness gives boundedness and a norm bound B≥1, by a finite subcover of growing balls. For each positive scale take a finite subcover by radius δ/2 balls. Their extended diameters are finite and at most δ; pad this finite cover with empty sets to bound Hscale.\"},{\"id\":\"T004\",\"statement\":\"0 < n → ∀ a : ℝ, (n : ℝ) < a → (∀ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ → Hscale a δ E = 0) ∧ Hmeasure a E = 0\",\"inputs\":[\"T003\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S004\"],\"explanation\":\"In the norm-bounded box use mesh-h coordinate cubes. Bound their number by (2B+3)^n h^(-n) and diameter by √n h. For a>n the resulting cost tends to zero as h decreases to zero. At any fixed scale sufficiently small meshes are admissible. This is the grid argument, not an invocation of the desired product theorem.\"},{\"id\":\"T005\",\"statement\":\"Bornology.IsBounded E ∧ (∀ (s δ : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → ∃ (k : ℕ) (U : Fin k → Set (V n)), E ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ (∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ) ∧ (∑ i, (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s) < ⊤) ∧ (∀ (s δ : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → Hscale s δ E < ⊤) ∧ 0 ≤ dimH E ∧ dimH E ≤ (n : ℝ≥0∞) ∧ dimH E < ⊤ ∧ (n = 0 → E = Set.univ ∧ dimH E = 0)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"T002\",\"T003\",\"T004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S003\",\"S004\"],\"explanation\":\"N002. Retain the compact finite-cover conclusions. For n>0 apply the zero-measure implication to every a>n and pass down to n. For n=0 nonemptiness makes E the entire singleton, whose positive-exponent singleton covers have zero cost; pass s down to zero. These bounds give finiteness.\"},{\"id\":\"T006\",\"statement\":\"n = 0 → dimH (cyl n E) ≤ dimH E + 1\",\"inputs\":[\"T002\",\"T005\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S005\"],\"explanation\":\"In zero ambient dimension E is the singleton. Use the pack copies of the N equal interval pieces in the Euclidean W 0 space. Their diameters are 1/N and a-cost is N^(1-a), tending to zero for a>1. Apply N001 and let a decrease to 1.\"},{\"id\":\"T007\",\"statement\":\"0 < n → ∀ (q r ε : ℝ), dimH E < ENNReal.ofReal q → 0 < r → r ≤ 1 → 0 < ε → ∃ U : ℕ → Set (V n), IsCover r E U ∧ (∀ i, (U i).Nonempty → 0 < Metric.ediam (U i)) ∧ coverCost q U < ENNReal.ofReal ε\",\"inputs\":[\"T002\",\"T005\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S006\"],\"explanation\":\"Obtain a cover of cost <ε/2 from zero q-measure. Keep positive-diameter members and replace zero-diameter nonempty members by small balls, assigning the original i-th member budget ε2^(-i-2). Since n>0 balls of sufficiently small positive radius have positive diameter and arbitrarily small q-cost. Empty slots can remain empty: this is the padded form of deleting them, with zero cost.\"},{\"id\":\"T008\",\"statement\":\"0 < n → ∀ (q δ ε : ℝ), dimH E < ENNReal.ofReal q → 0 < δ → 0 < ε → Hscale (q + 1) δ (cyl n E) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (2 * (Real.sqrt 2) ^ (q + 1) * ε)\",\"inputs\":[\"T007\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S007\"],\"explanation\":\"Apply T007 at r=min(1,δ/√2). For each nonempty member use ceil(1/diam U_i) interval pieces. With Euclidean coordinates the product diameter is ≤√2 diam U_i, and ceil(1/diam U_i)≤2/diam U_i. Enumerate the countable family, ignoring empty slots, to obtain the cost bound. Powers and diameter estimates use the finite real representatives guaranteed by the finite-scale condition.\"},{\"id\":\"T009\",\"statement\":\"dimH (cyl n E) ≤ dimH E + 1\",\"inputs\":[\"T002\",\"T005\",\"T006\",\"T008\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"N003. For n>0 let ε decrease to zero in T008, then take the supremum of scales and apply N001. The bounds for every real q>D imply the bound D+1 using finite D. Combine with T006 for n=0.\"},{\"id\":\"T010\",\"statement\":\"∀ (s δ ε : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → 0 < ε → ∀ Vc : ℕ → Set (W n), IsCover δ (cyl n E) Vc → ∃ J : ℕ → Set ℝ, (∀ i, IsOpen (J i) ∧ projT n '' Vc i ⊆ J i ∧ MeasureTheory.volume (J i) ≤ Metric.ediam (Vc i) + ENNReal.ofReal ε * (1 / 2 : ℝ≥0∞) ^ (i + 1) / (1 + (Metric.ediam (Vc i)) ^ s)) ∧ (∀ t ∈ unitI, Hscale s δ E ≤ ∑' i, (J i).indicator (fun _ : ℝ => (Metric.ediam (Vc i)) ^ s) t) ∧ (∀ i, Measurable ((J i).indicator (fun _ : ℝ => (Metric.ediam (Vc i)) ^ s)))\",\"inputs\":[\"T005\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S009\",\"S010\",\"S011\"],\"explanation\":\"c=Hscale(s,δ,E) is finite by N002. Both coordinate projections decrease Euclidean distances. Enclose each nonempty real projection in the open interval obtained by enlarging its infimum and supremum by η_i/2, with η_i=ε2^(-i-1)/(1+ρ_i^s); put J_i=∅ in the empty case. Finite scale ensures these endpoints and coefficients are finite. The displayed ENNReal error is the embedding of η_i. For each t∈I, the selected first-coordinate projections cover E; compare costs to get the pointwise bound. Open J_i make the indicators measurable; no cover member is assumed measurable.\"},{\"id\":\"T011\",\"statement\":\"∀ (s δ ε : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → 0 < ε → ∀ Vc : ℕ → Set (W n), IsCover δ (cyl n E) Vc → Hscale s δ E ≤ coverCost (s + 1) Vc + ENNReal.ofReal ε\",\"inputs\":[\"T005\",\"T010\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S012\"],\"explanation\":\"Integrate the pointwise bound against Lebesgue measure restricted to I, whose mass is one. Apply lintegral_tsum to the nonnegative measurable indicators, evaluate indicator integrals, and bound volume(J_i∩I) by volume(J_i)≤ρ_i+η_i. Distribute the nonnegative sums, use ρ_i^s ρ_i=ρ_i^(s+1), and sum the geometric error budget to ε. Empty members have zero powers since s>0. All comparisons remain valid for infinite sums.\"},{\"id\":\"T012\",\"statement\":\"∀ (s δ : ℝ), 0 < s → 0 < δ → Hscale s δ E ≤ Hscale (s + 1) δ (cyl n E)\",\"inputs\":[\"T011\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S013\"],\"explanation\":\"N004. For each arbitrary cover, if its cost is infinite the bound is immediate; otherwise let ε decrease to zero in T011. Then take the infimum over covers. The auxiliary intervals may depend on ε but the two sides of the limiting inequality do not.\"},{\"id\":\"T013\",\"statement\":\"∀ s : ℝ, 0 < s → ENNReal.ofReal s < dimH E → ENNReal.ofReal (s + 1) ≤ dimH (cyl n E)\",\"inputs\":[\"T002\",\"T005\",\"T012\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S014\"],\"explanation\":\"For 0<s<D use N001 to get infinite s-measure of E. Take the scale supremum of N004 to obtain infinite (s+1)-measure of the cylinder; N001 gives the dimension bound.\"},{\"id\":\"T014\",\"statement\":\"0 < dimH E → dimH E + 1 ≤ dimH (cyl n E)\",\"inputs\":[\"T005\",\"T013\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S015\"],\"explanation\":\"N005. Since D is finite and positive, positive real s<D approach its real representative from below. Take the supremum of the bounds s+1≤dimH F.\"},{\"id\":\"T015\",\"statement\":\"dimH unitI ≤ 1\",\"inputs\":[\"T002\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S016\"],\"explanation\":\"Use the N equal closed interval subdivision covers, with mesh 1/N and a-cost N^(1-a) tending to zero for a>1. Apply N001 and let a decrease to one.\"},{\"id\":\"T016\",\"statement\":\"∀ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ → ∀ U : ℕ → Set ℝ, IsCover δ unitI U → (1 : ℝ≥0∞) ≤ ∑' i, Metric.ediam (U i)\",\"inputs\":[],\"source_steps\":[\"S017\"],\"explanation\":\"For any ε>0 enclose each nonempty bounded cover member in an open interval of length ≤diam(U_i)+ε2^(-i-1), taking empty members to ∅. The intervals cover I. Use its Lebesgue measure one, countable subadditivity, and the open interval volume formula. Sum the geometric error and let ε decrease to zero, handling infinite sums separately.\"},{\"id\":\"T017\",\"statement\":\"dimH unitI = 1 ∧ ∀ s : ℝ, 0 < s → s < 1 → Hmeasure s unitI = ⊤\",\"inputs\":[\"T002\",\"T015\",\"T016\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S018\"],\"explanation\":\"For 0<s<1 and mesh δ>0 use ρ_i^s≥δ^(s-1)ρ_i, including zero diameters. T016 gives Hscale(s,δ,I)≥δ^(s-1). This tends to infinity as δ decreases to zero, proving infinite measure. N001 and s increasing to one give the lower dimension bound, combined with T015.\"},{\"id\":\"T018\",\"statement\":\"∀ (b δ : ℝ), 0 < b → 0 < δ → Hscale b δ unitI ≤ Hscale b δ (cyl n E)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S019\"],\"explanation\":\"Choose x0∈E and use t↦pack n x0 t, whose Euclidean distance equals |t-u| in every n. Pull each arbitrary cylinder cover back to subsets of I. These cover I, decrease diameters, and have zero cost on empty preimages. Compare costs then take the infimum. This explicitly proves the required monotonicity rather than using the product-dimension conclusion.\"},{\"id\":\"T019\",\"statement\":\"dimH E = 0 → (1 : ℝ≥0∞) ≤ dimH (cyl n E) ∧ (1 : ℝ≥0∞) = dimH E + 1\",\"inputs\":[\"T002\",\"T017\",\"T018\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S019\"],\"explanation\":\"N006. Supremize T018 over scales. For every 0<a<1, T017 gives infinite a-measure of I, hence of the cylinder. Apply N001 and let a increase to one. Under D=0, one equals D+1, including n=0.\"},{\"id\":\"T020\",\"statement\":\"dimH (cyl n E) = dimH E + 1\",\"inputs\":[\"T005\",\"T009\",\"T014\",\"T019\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S020\"],\"explanation\":\"P. Since D is nonnegative, split into D>0 and D=0. T014 and T019 give the same lower bound in the two cases; T009 is the upper bound. Apply antisymmetry.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T020\",\"source_outputs\":{\"N001\":\"T002\",\"N002\":\"T005\",\"N003\":\"T009\",\"N004\":\"T012\",\"N005\":\"T014\",\"N006\":\"T019\",\"P\":\"T020\"},\"endpoint_correspondence\":{\"P\":{\"mode\":\"direct\",\"explanation\":\"Parameters n:ℕ and E:Set(EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) range over exactly all original n≥0 and Euclidean subsets. H001 is precisely nonemptiness and H002 precisely compactness, with no further assumptions. W n is the Euclidean coordinate space indexed by the n original coordinates and one final coordinate; its squared distance is the sum of the n squared coordinate differences plus the last squared difference. Thus cyl n E is exactly E×[0,1] under the original Euclidean identification, not a max-norm product. This works when Fin 0 is empty as well. Native dimH is the specified extended-nonnegative supremum definition, and T001 identifies the unnormalized cover measure. The conclusion is exactly dim_H(E×[0,1])=dim_H(E)+1 in that codomain; T005 proves finiteness rather than assuming it. No second metric representation or conversion theorem is required.\"}}}}","status":"completed"}}

